Integration notes for impl/stop-diff-impl
=========================================

This branch does not build on its own and is not meant to. gitrepo's `run` and
`Root` helpers live in internal/gitrepo/gitrepo.go on impl/baseline-mark, and
filemod.Observed lives on impl/observed-extract, so `go build ./...` here fails
with `undefined: run` until those are merged. What follows is what integration
needs on top of the merge.

THE MERGE IS FOUR-WAY, and the order below is the one that was verified:

    impl/engine-skeleton        (base)
    impl/baseline-mark          gitrepo.go, the baseline, readmark
    impl/observed-extract       filemod.Observed and the presence checks
    impl/fingerprint-skip       Skip/Record, so blessings and retained
                                refusals persist across cycles
    impl/stop-diff-impl         this branch

Two facts about the bases that are not obvious from the branch names:

  * impl/observed-extract branches from 9a6053c, NOT from the engine-skeleton
    head. `git merge-base impl/engine-skeleton impl/observed-extract` is the
    check.

  * impl/fingerprint-skip conflicts with the first three in
    services/sloprail/hookio.go, services/sloprail/hookio_test.go and
    services/sloprail/session_id.go. These are mostly doc-comment supersets,
    but NOT entirely: the two sides disagreed about whether a session id of
    "." or ".." is refused. It is not, and must not be — the ".jsonl" suffix is
    concatenated BEFORE filepath.Join, so "." becomes "..jsonl" and ".."
    becomes "...jsonl", both ordinary filenames inside the project directory.
    The separator guard is what stops a real traversal ("../../etc/passwd"),
    and it is retained. Keep HEAD's errNoRecord branch in stableID; keep
    HEAD's BelongsToSession/BelongsToTree cross-checks in transcript().

CONFLICT: tests/e2e/harness/harness.go

Merging this branch after impl/baseline-mark conflicts in the harness. It is a
textual adjacency collision and nothing more — baseline-mark appends GitInit,
Git, Meta, sessionDBPath, transcriptPath and dataHome at the end of the file,
and this branch appends WriteFile and Exists at the same point. Neither touches
the other's methods.

It union-resolves, but NOT by taking both sides verbatim: the conflict region
cuts through dataHome's body, so a naive union drops the closing brace of its
switch and the file no longer parses. Keep both blocks and restore the `}` that
closes dataHome before WriteFile begins.

The harness hunk below carries that resolution, and adds BlockingErrors, which
the e2e tests for a Post refusal need.

WHY BlockingErrors READS THE TRANSCRIPT

Measured on this harness, of the ways a Stop hook can refuse:

    exit 2, text on stderr             blocks, and the text arrives
    exit 0, {"decision":"block"}       blocks, and the reason arrives
    exit 1, text on stderr             does NOT block, nothing arrives
    exit 0, silent                     does NOT block

Both blocking forms deliver their words as a `hook_blocking_error` attachment
in the conversation record, never on the result stream. An e2e test asserting
on Result.Output would be asserting on a channel the text never travels.

